  "content_en": "The Biography of Empress Xiaohui Zhang of the Han Dynasty (with postscript) This should be the biography of Empress Xiaohui Zhang mentioned in the commentary. LU5 Novel Network is indeed very gorgeous, I love it too. It is said to have been commissioned by people of the Eastern Jin Dynasty. I tried reading \"The Biography of Empress Xiaohui Zhang of the Han Dynasty\" in the past, and I suspected that the narrative was a little short. Everything recorded in the biography is all about Empress Dowager Lu. I also read the \"Five Elements Chronicles\", which records the disaster of the weaving room in the fourth year of Emperor Hui's reign. He thought it was a sign of Empress Zhang's loss of virtue and a sign of desolation. Disasters in the husband's palace are a common occurrence, but it is unreasonable to attribute the blame to the newly established Zhang Hou. Later, he entered the palace as a child, but he was widowed at an early age. He was not interested in foreign affairs, and even the affairs in the palace were in charge of the Empress Dowager Lu. It was in vain for the ministers to move the angry Empress Zhang and set up a secluded Beigong because of the Lu family. It would be in vain for historians to take advantage of the hidden world and blame it for their lack of morality. It was Min Ranzhi who used it, and then he studied the chronicles and biographies of \"History\" and \"Han\", studied all the histories, searched for barnyard records, and also read novels. He picked up more than fifty kinds of them and wrote a piece of \"Wai Zhuan\". For more than ten years, I have not dared to come out. When I heard about the robbery of the Han Dynasty Mausoleum in Yongjia, some of them were noted by Gao Hui, Wen Jing and the Four Dynasties of the Han Dynasty, and spread to Jiangzuo. After an urgent visit, I obtained three volumes of \"Xiang Nu Jing\", two volumes of \"Records of Concubines of Xianghan Palace\", and \"Genealogy of the Zhang Family in Guanzhong\". They were read together and occasionally used to supplement the previous biography. The peerless virtue of Zhang Empress was related to the reason why she was falsely accused of seclusion at that time. Empress Xiaohui of the Han Dynasty, her surname was Yan, her courtesy name was Meng Yu, and her nickname was Shu. Huidi's sister is the eldest daughter of Princess Lu Yuan. When the first emperor was the pavilion chief, he married Empress Lu and gave birth to a daughter and a son. The male is Emperor Xiaohui, and the female is Princess Lu Yuan. In the second year of Emperor Gaodi's reign, the Han army was defeated at Pengcheng, and Empress Lu was captured by Chu. Emperor Gao met Emperor Hui and his princess on the road and carried them on their way, but their horses were tired and they were captured behind. The emperor crumpled his two sons and wanted to abandon them, but Teng Gong often came down to collect them and carried them slowly. Facing Yongshu Naichi, the soldier was able to escape between Xiayi, and then brought him into the pass. At that time, Emperor Hui was six years old and the princess was twelve years old. In the sixth month of the Han Dynasty, the capital of the Han Dynasty was Yueyang. He established the Tai Tai and ordered the princes to serve as guards. The princess was very virtuous and kind, and Emperor Gao loved her very much. The emperor said: \"We should choose a good son-in-law for him.\" Zhang Erzhi Ao Fang lived in the Han Dynasty in Wei. He was fourteen years old and had a very handsome appearance. Xu Negative Prime Minister said: I should be a king and a marquis, and give birth to a daughter with excellent virtues and beauty. Ao Wei's letter. The emperor's beloved Ao Dujin was named Princess. In the fourth month of summer in the fifth year, Princess Aoshang became the king of Zhao, and in the seventh month of autumn, she moved to Zhao, and the princess became the queen. On the third day of the third month of the sixth year, a daughter was born in Handan. Five-colored clouds covered the palace, and the sound of fairy music could be faintly heard in the air. Ao was born charming, so she named her Yan. When he was several years old, he became gentle and quiet. He had no teeth and could not leave the pavilion. Zhang Ao said to the princess: \"A Yan is kind to others and behaves dignifiedly. Her future blessings are immeasurable, but she is afraid that if she is too kind and kind, she will be deceived by others.\" In the ninth year, Zhang Ao was deposed as Marquis Xuanping, and his family members all moved to Chang'an. Emperor Huigao used Lou Jingce to marry Princess Lu Yuan to the Huns. The princess cried to Zhang Ao day and night, and A Yan also held the princess's clothes and cried. Emperor Gao took pity on him when he heard about it, and Empress Lu tried her best to speak to the emperor, but she stopped. When A Yan was five or six years old, her appearance was extremely beautiful. Whenever his mother came in and out of the palace, Emperor Gao often ordered Mrs. Qi to hold her in her arms, feed her with fruit bait, and say to her: \"Although you are unparalleled in beauty, this girl will be beyond your reach in ten years.\" When Emperor Hui was the queen, he married a certain daughter of a meritorious official as his concubine. The concubine also often hugged Ayan for joy. When Emperor Hui came to the throne, he did not have three years of mourning and could not establish a queen. When the concubine passed away, the emperor was moved by the change of the pig. He specializes in hiding his secrets and entertains himself with wine and sex. There are many beauties in the harem, and they dote on beautiful boys and children, lying down and getting up with them. During the reign of Emperor Hui, all the ministers and ministers were painted with powder and wore crowns with turtlenecks, which was the custom of Hong children. After the establishment of the emperor, he wanted to visit the daughter of a famous nobleman with outstanding grace and virtue. The Queen Mother often felt pity for Ao Zhi, and wanted to marry Ao's daughter to the emperor. She said to the emperor: \"A Yan is the nephew of the emperor's family, the daughter of the royal family, a noble species in the world, truly unparalleled, and her grace and virtue are unparalleled in ancient and modern times. I have chosen a woman.\" For several years, no one has surpassed this woman. \"The emperor said: \"What is the order of good ethics, and she is still young?\" The queen mother said: \"You are too young to grow up, and your nephew is not among the five ethics. Why don't you hear that Duke Wen of Jin wants to marry Wen Ying?\" The emperor obeyed the order and ordered the ministers to discuss the ceremony. In the spring of the third year, the Empress Dowager sent Changle Shaofu and Zongzheng to accept the emperor's proposal, with a bundle of silk and wild goose biscuits, four horses, and to ask for an audience with his daughter. Eight people from Fu Mu supported the girl, and she stood facing the south in full attire. She is only ten years old, and the Queen Mother is afraid that people will judge her young age. The messenger claimed to be twelve years old, and when he asked for his name, he told the temple that all the rituals were the same. However, Yan's physique is already as good as that of Twelve or Thirteen. Everyone who saw it stared at him and licked his tongue, thinking that he was a fairy. It is also reported that Ping Hou's daughter has a pure appearance, is diligent in etiquette, and has the virtue of maternal etiquette., with a graceful appearance, it is suitable to inherit Tianzuo and serve in the ancestral temple. The prime minister, Taiwei Bo, the imperial censor Yao, and the Taishi used Tailuo to report to the temple, and used rituals to divine the auspicious month and day. The questions about the name, the acceptance of auspiciousness, the acceptance of the levy, the date of request, and the grand ceremony were all determined by Taifu Shusun Tong. The betrothal ceremony included twelve horses and twenty thousand catties of gold, which was unprecedented since ancient times. Since Han Dynasty established the latter, it must be based on the story of Emperor Xiaohui accepting the queen. The younger brother Yan, who was still young, saw a lot of gold lying on the bed, so he rushed in and said, \"Sister Yan, the emperor has bought you.\" Princess Lu Yuan scolded her and said, \"Don't say more, little girl.\" Yan Nai took her sister's hand and said, \"Sister, why don't you go out to see?\" The Han Dynasty followed the Qin system, and every time a concubine was admitted, a female official who knew how to look after her would be sent to examine her. In autumn and August, the imperial edict (this bird) was issued to the marquis Xu Fu to the Xuanping Marquis. The one who promised to be negative was an old woman from Hanoi, and he was the one who granted the title of marquis because of his kindness. He led Nu Yan to the secret room and bathed her. Looking closely at Yan's face, she is long and slightly round, white and flawless, her cheeks are plump and shaped like a full moon, her eyebrows are like phoenix eyes, her temples are like dragons, her ears are big and drooping on her shoulders, and she is as white as her face. The chin is wide and round, and the light can tell people, the chest is flat, the shoulders are round and upright, the back is slightly thick, the waist is slender, the texture is greasy and clean, the fat is thin, and there are no hemorrhoids or ulcers, no black wounds, and other private diseases of the mouth, nose, armpits, and feet. Xu negative one by one, urging Yan to thank the emperor for ten thousand years. Yan was embarrassed and refused, so he persuaded him for the fourth time. Then he bowed slowly and whispered that he would be the emperor for ten thousand years. The negative form was secretly presented to the Queen Mother and Emperor Hui. The emperor was overjoyed after seeing it and paid it to the palace historian. In the tenth month of winter at Renyin, the imperial edict was sent to Prime Minister Xiangcan and the imperial censor Yao to welcome the queen Xuanping Houdi. The queen's dress is denuded at the top, with a deep collar and wide sleeves, and a gauze belt. The dress is so long that it touches the floor, with no feet visible. Wearing a dragon and phoenix bead crown, swaying with gold and hairpins, he bowed to the Zhang family's temple. When applying make-up, you should use fake hair as a rule. From now on, Fu Mu will be as handsome as a cloud and please leave with Princess Lu Yuan. Zhang Ao carried his daughter into the car, called the police, and entered the front hall of Weiyang Palace. Tianlinxuan, accompanied by hundreds of officials. To the north of the queen, the etiquette officer finished reading the book. Queen Liusu knelt down and bowed three times, and the female officials led her to the emperor to express her gratitude. Then he bowed down and there was no sound for a long time. The female official taught it by ear, and was later called \"Concubine Zhang Yan, congratulations to the Emperor for ten thousand years.\" Its subtle charm is like the breeze blowing the flute, and like the first call of an oriole. The emperor was moved and stood up. Taiwei Bo was awarded the seal and ribbon, and the regular servants knelt down to receive it, and he was conferred the title of female official. The female officer led the queen, who bowed down and called her concubine again. After thanking her for her kindness, she ascended the throne. All the officials took their seats and bowed before retreating. The empress entered the middle palace in a soft carriage, and the officials established themselves as emperors. Instead of marrying into the family of a meritorious official, they were selfish about their nephews. All of them had a sense of injustice. After arriving at the middle palace, the walls are all painted with gold, pepper is fragrant, embellished with pearls for curtains, carved sapphire for tables, sandalwood for the bed, inlaid with corals, red rhinestones for the tents, decorated with emeralds, brocade quilts and embroidered pillows, all with woven gold dragons and phoenixes. The other displays are filled with treasures and play, which are so bright that they cannot be described. The emperor and his queen performed the ceremony of union. Later, she followed the teachings of a female official and worshiped the emperor, claiming to be her niece Ayan and congratulating his majesty the uncle for ten thousand years. The emperor smiled and said: \"You still call me \"ye\" from the front.\" He also drank the wine from the gold bottle. Later, he was stunned and couldn't drink, so he barely finished a bottle. In the evening, I sat on the bed. The emperor held the candle and looked carefully, and saw the pair of servant girls hanging behind her. They were pure and beautiful, without any makeup or powder on them. Their color was like the morning glow reflecting the snow, or like pear blossoms carrying the rain. The positions of their various bodies were extremely wonderful. He bowed down in shame and fear, with mouths on both sides, slightly dizzy like finger marks, like the waves of the waves. The emperor said to the queen: \"I always avoided suspicion because of your nephew, and I didn't look closely. Unexpectedly, your heart is so pleasant that it is so extreme.\" At that time, the queen was ten years old. Although he was in the middle palace, the emperor did not stay overnight. The affairs of the palace are left to the beauties and elders of the harem to take charge of. Seeing that the queen had no power, the harem tried to invade and insult her, and privately discussed: \"Although Zhang Shu occupies an honorable position, she is really a virgin. And after entering the palace, how can we be afraid of us.\" Five days later, the queen mother presented the meal to the table, bowed and held her breath, feeling solemn and happy. After the emperor went to the Changle Palace in the East, every time he passed through the streets, he would visit many people and build a new road to belong to the Changle Palace. Every time after going out, the maid first moves the chariot into the inner room, then sits in it, puts on the curtains, and then walks around. Although people from the eunuch palace may not be able to see the back. After that, every morning when I was doing my makeup in the mirror, there was a little bird with colorful ornaments flying outside the curtain and singing, like the cloud \"Wrap up in the quiet room\", \"Wrap up in the quiet room\", and it stayed like this for more than ten years. Later, after migrating to the North Palace, the birds never came again. In the spring and March of the fourth year, Emperor Hui was twenty. On the eleventh day of the following year, the emperor performed a crowning ceremony and led the queen to the Gaomiao. The peacocks and white cranes in the palace will dance when they see you. After Princess Lu Yuan came to the palace for a visit, she was given a welcome gift like a family member, expressing her attachment to her mother. The princess pointed to Emperor Hui and said, \"A Yan, are you satisfied?\" The emperor said, \"A Yan is not like my eldest sister, but she is very similar to Marquis Xuan Ping, which makes my sixth palace Fendai look less beautiful. Her quiet, intelligent and willing nature is the same as that of her eldest sister.\"At that time, his younger brother Zhang Yan was at his side. The emperor held him in his arms and said, \"This son's physique is quite similar to that of his sister. If he were a woman, he would be a beautiful woman.\" Every morning when the emperor got up, he would go to the Jiao Room to watch the queen take a bath (page 1). A palace official said: \"The queen's appearance is so beautiful that she wants to compete with the white jade plate.\" He also said: \"The queen looks like a Xuan Pinghou, but her appearance is smaller.\" Because of the joke, she called her \"Zhang Gong\". When Fu Mu saw that the emperor was coming, he would first hold a golden spit bowl, fill it with crape myrtle dew, and then rinse his mouth with sandalwood. The emperor often held it in his arms and put it on his knees. He counted his white teeth, forty in number, and rubbed vermilion into his back lip. One day, the emperor came to the harem and took off his clothes. The two palace people washed the queen's feet. The emperor sat looking at her and smiled and said: \"Ayan is young but her feet are long, almost as long as mine.\" He also said to the palace people: \"The queen's shin and tarsus are round and white and delicate. Who among your generation can match her.\"... In the first month of the spring of the seventh year, Emperor Hui was hunting in Shangyuan. The queen and all the beauties rode and followed her, all dressed like men, their robes colored crimson, yellow or green. The back body is made of royal fox white fur, the color of the clothes is dark green, and the skirt is pure yellow. She wears a red brocade robe on the outside, and wipes her forehead with red gauze. She is galloping around, and the flowers and plants are shining, all of them are as graceful as a twenty-eight-year-old princess. Those who see her don't know that she is a concubine. Then he was particularly stunning. He undressed and went to the toilet. A wild pig broke into his back and tore his lower clothes. There was a slight injury to his buttocks. The emperor was frightened and frightened, so he stabbed the pig with his sword and killed him. All the beauties congratulated him. After his lower clothes were torn and torn, he was exposed in a hurry and unconsciously. The emperor smiled and pointed at it and said, \"How fat and white are you?\" The latter was shocked, embarrassed and at a loss. He hurriedly called the maid to get under his clothes, his cheeks were dizzy, and he remained silent for a long time. In the fourth month of summer, the queen went out with silkworms in her royal ceremonial attire, riding on a luan and chariot, riding a four-horse horse, Zhang Qingyu, and nine dragon flags. The wife of the Taiwei rode in the imperial palace, and the wife of the Imperial servant went to the front. The Chang'an order was followed, and the golden and yellow axes were used. The queen gathered mulberries in the Silkworm Palace, held three pots in the Cocoon Pavilion, and returned to the palace after paying homage. That day, there were so many people watching in Chang'an, and all the women of the hero's family sighed in admiration and said: \"Zhang Ao's daughter is so lucky, I really regret not being able to see her face.\" When Emperor Hui heard about it, he became angry with Marquis Biyang and sent him to prison, where he was about to kill him and then released him. The Queen Mother felt ashamed and resented the fact that there was no emperor and there were many beauties in the harem, so she decided to denounce all the beauties in order to get the Queen to be favored by Zhuan Fang. The emperor was very worried and had no idea, so he expressed his condolences to the queen. In order to plan to sleep with her, she was of a good-natured nature and did not know jealousy. She was always happy with the Queen Mother, so she cried and said that all the beauties were not guilty. Concubine Yan thought she was too thin and could not give birth, so the Queen Mother stopped. In May, the Queen Mother heard that the beauty in the harem was pregnant, and she became angry and planned to kill her. In order to persuade the queen, the queen mother suddenly came up with a plan, so that the queen would pretend to be pregnant for several months, and when the beautiful woman gave birth to a boy, she would be named the queen's son and become the queen. Later, she had no choice but to follow her advice and said to her mother, Princess Lu Yuan: \"Yan Yumei has always been deeply ashamed of the petty things she did. However, if Yan is absent, the Queen Mother will never be happy, and the emperors will also be in danger. The emperor will be depressed and sick. Well, (face page) Yan is like this, to entertain the Queen Mother, to protect the emperor, and to harmonize the two palaces, and the emperor bows his ears. \"The queen mother issued an edict that the queen will be pregnant until the end of the month, so she can avoid the lunar calendar.\" The emperor also did not come to the harem for months, and the queen lived in seclusion, never leaving the dormitory. One of the maids was cunning and whispered to each other, \"The Queen is going to give birth to a wife, but why is her belly not big?\" Beauty in June gave birth to a boy, and the Queen Mother sent him to take him, wrap him in a blanket, send him to the harem, and kill his mother. That day, the Queen Mother sent Gong'e to the Queen Mother to pretend that she had abdominal pain. Soon after, the croak was already in her arms. He offered sacrifices to the ancestral temple and established him as Tai Tai, and the officials congratulated him. Three days later, the queen's envoy gave the beauty medicine, Wenqi, and a hundred catties of gold. Perhaps it was said that the Queen Mother had already killed her, but she was so frightened that she went to meet him with tears in her eyes, her red sleeves were all wet, and she secretly told Emperor Hui, \"The reason why I have endured this is because I want to save this person. I still see him being killed. Isn't it because of bad luck?\" At that time, Emperor Hui's harem had six children, and the child named after him was the youngest. After caressing them all as if they were their own children, and taking care of their mothers at all times. That year, the emperor's younger brother, King Huainan, came to court. The king's mother was a beauty in the Zhang Ao family. Ao Xian was the first emperor to be a king, so he was the closest to the Zhang family. As for the emperor Hui, I would like to go to the queen. The emperor said: \"Your sister-in-law is not even old enough to have hairpins. She is simple, naive and fearful of people. She is like a virgin. She can do it.\" He agreed to her request. The king knelt down and bowed respectfully, and then bowed in reply inside the curtain. He wore a pendant ring and made a ringing sound. He stood up and solemnly said, \"Nine uncles are fine.\" Then he sat upright without saying a word or even looking up. The king retreated and said to the man: \"My sister-in-law is the most beautiful woman in ancient and modern times, and also the most kind person.\" In August, the emperor did not hesitate, and the queen asked about her illness. The emperor suddenly sent the queen to get on the bed, touch her breasts and sigh: \"Ah Yan has grown up now, and I can't bear to let go of you. However, your body is so thick that I am afraid that you will become thinner for me in the future. There is such a person who cannot live happily as a couple for a day, and he is also a husband.\" Wuyin, the emperor died in Weiyang Palace at the age of twenty-three.When he was fourteen years later, he cried like a ritual, bathed like a ritual, and then stopped. The princes, kings and ministers raised their highnesses, and the queen was in the palace, facing east and west, all crying. All the concubines, princesses and eldest wives came to the crying hall from the queen, no less than a hundred people. Princess Lu Yuan also joined Yan. When the officials heard it from a distance, their voices were delicate and they cried in sorrow. Looking from afar, she is the youngest, and her color is stunning, making her look like a queen. The back eyes were as red and swollen as peaches, the screen was gone, and the whole body was covered with linen. They became more beautiful and shone with brilliance, making everyone in the palace tremble. After the Queen Mother came to the throne, the Queen Mother came to the court and took the throne, and she always lived in the main hall of Weiyang Palace. Later known as Queen Xiaohui, she still lived in the Jiao Fang of the Central Palace. Every day, the Queen Mother came to court. She wanted to take advantage of this moment to punish all the meritorious officials, but she stopped with bitter remonstrances. Its language is secret and unknown to outsiders. At that time, Zhang Qing, the great visitor, came in and out of the Queen Mother's bed. Every time he went to see the Queen Mother, Zhang Qing saw that she was walking around like a virgin, not daring to say anything to her without asking, not daring to sit down when she was not ordered to do so, and talking about Zhao Yin. The person who spoke to you thought that she had not seen anything in the picture, and said: \"If you want to know Queen Zhang, but look at her younger brother Zhang Yan, she is already ten to five or six.\" On the fifteenth day of the following year, Princess Lu Yuan passed away, and the Queen Mother sent the queen home to attend her mother's funeral. Later, when he was young and weak, he lived in the house and was depressed and sad, so he composed a song and said: \"As a child, I entered the pepper room and waited silently for the new year to see the late emperor. The late emperor passed away in the near future, and I stayed in the empty bed after holding the uncultivated child. I enjoyed the good night with candles, and admired the flying giants. I complained about wealth and ridicule for entertainment, which is not as good as the wretchedness of the common people. When the night is long, the moon shines with a weak shadow. We chatted and thought about the past, as if my uncle was here; the wind came back, and I suddenly felt as if someone had died. I wiped my tears from my clothes, and wandered on my feet. The chickens sang in chorus to report the dawn, thinking about my uncle's heart and soul; I hope that after death, I will be in the same place, and I will worship the clear light in the ground.\" So the Empress Dowager ordered the right prime minister to supervise the Weiyang Palace and live in the palace to serve the Empress Dowager. Everything in the palace belongs to Yan, no matter how big or small it is. The Marquis of Piyang pursued Emperor Hui, and Queen Xiaohui took the daily diet and cut off more than half of it. Later, Shao Ai wanted to poison him to repay Emperor Hui, so he bribed the queen's maid and asked him about his personal affairs. A maid said: \"I have served the Queen for the longest time, and I know it quite well. The Queen does not stand lamely, nor does she sit in a lazy manner. She lives at regular intervals, walks and stops at regular intervals, and eats and drinks more than a normal person. She plays well, which is different from the customs of the times. She coughs and spits on the ground, and the grass grows every time, and the fragrance is as fragrant as orchids. Although there is no slight sweat in the hot summer, there is no slight odor in the feces, and there is no snoring when sleeping. She treats us neatly and kindly. , but there is a little bit of joking, and the postscript says: There are two chapters in the biography of Queen Xiaohui, so the author's surname is not mentioned in the biography. , but it is known that it was written by someone in the Eastern Jin Dynasty. He searched extensively and tried to rectify the case of Ban Shi and rectify A Yan's injustice. It contains thousands of words and can be read together in the following chapters. It is probably written by one person and can be read together.",
